WEBVTT

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.990
I'll beat to death anyone who doesn't observe the value of life.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>I'll beat to death anyone who
 doesn't observe the value of life.</i>

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.250
<b>Episode 6</b>

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.250
<b>Operation 
Errand Run</b>

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.620
<i>I'm so busy all the time.</i>

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:29.650
<i>I can never find time to go out.</i>

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:31.260
What shall I do?

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:33.260
Want me to help?

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.710
Rampo-san.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.270
You're too busy healing people
 to buy supplies, right?

00:00:38.270 --> 00:00:41.390
Would you really do that for me?

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.400
I'll find someone to go for you.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.420
So... you aren't the one going.

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:48.550
That's right.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.290
Well, okay. Thank you.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.220
I need...

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.740
Medical charts and scissors, right?

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.330
I'm impressed, Rampo-san.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.860
<b>Charts</b>

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.860
<b>Scissors</b>

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.170
You really do see through me.

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:02.310
Kenji-kun.

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:04.650
Yes? How can I help?

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:07.320
Could you pick some things up at the store?

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.410
Some errands?

00:01:08.410 --> 00:01:11.720
Yosano-san says she wants
 some charts and scissors.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.810
Got it. I'll go.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:15.170
Thanks!

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.930
Shoot, I was supposed to go to a scene.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.180
I won't make it in time 
if I go shopping first.

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.520
Is there a problem?

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:27.100
Kunikida-san! I'm glad I ran into you.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.940
Well, what's happening is...

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.680
I see.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.210
Very well. I'll do the shopping for you.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.500
Really?

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.160
Thank you!

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:40.830
So, what is it that she needs?

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.770
Let's see, uh...

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:43.910
<b>Charts</b>

00:01:43.330 --> 00:01:43.910
<b>Scissors</b>

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:45.120
<b>Charts</b>

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:45.120
<b>Scissors</b>

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.080
<b>Short 
Ribs</b>

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.080
<b>Skirt 
Steaks</b>

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.080
She needs short ribs and skirt steaks.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:51.460
<b>Short Ribs  Skirt Steaks)</b>

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:54.700
Just what is Yosano-sensei 
going to do with those?

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:57.060
Maybe she's grilling some meat.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.300
Didn't you say she needed supplies?

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:01.470
Well, all right. I'll take care of it.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:03.420
Thank you.

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:08.360
Oi, Dazai.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.230
Get up, you blockhead.

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:13.230
Is it morning already?

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.400
Buck up.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.000
I have work for you.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.610
I'm busy right now.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:20.920
How are you busy?!

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:23.240
We have some important errands to run.

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.740
Be grateful for the task.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.120
What do I have to buy?

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:33.420
Yosano-sensei requires short ribs
 and skirt steaks for grilling.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.630
Why?!

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.070
Maybe she has a patient who's going
 to die if they don't eat grilled meat!

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:40.380
I wish I had that sickness.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:43.510
Anyway, that's what I've been told, so do it!

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.970
What a slave driver.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:49.430
Who might have some time right now?

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.400
Yosano-sensei needs some supplies?

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:55.580
That's right.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:58.240
Kunikida-kun has designated <i>you</i> to do it.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.280
What do I need to buy?

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.650
Um...

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:05.280
Yosano-sensei requires short ribs
 and skirt steaks for grilling.

00:03:07.490 --> 00:03:12.290
<b>Cow</b>

00:03:08.350 --> 00:03:09.170
A cow.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.290
That sounds like a lot more
 work than buying supplies!

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.590
Thanks, man.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:15.110
Y-You're sure about this?

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:16.020
Yeah.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.470
I'm going to do it.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:18.380
Yeah.

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:19.800
I'm going to buy a cow.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.550
I never lied.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:23.300
<b>A few days later</b>

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.510
It looks like Hanako.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:27.060
This takes me back to my days in the village.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.600
Do you think it'll eat this?

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.940
If it were a goat, maybe.

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:31.810
I mean, you shouldn't 
feed goats paper, either.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.260
See! That was wrong!

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.690
I did have a feeling 
that wasn't quite right.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:40.300
<i>Hanako the Second ended up
 being taken good care of.</i>

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:44.040
Well, jeez.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.960
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.960
<b>Finders
 Kyouka's</b>

00:04:04.940 --> 00:04:05.720
A kitten!

00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:07.770
Did you find it, Kyouka-chan?

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:09.650
Yeah, in the alleyway.

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.270
It has a collar.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.850
Maybe it can't find its way home.

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.590
Hey!

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.030
It seems to like you, Atsushi-kun.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.910
Maybe it thinks he's a fellow cat.

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:27.360
I'm a <i>tiger!</i>

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:28.160
Nyarr!

00:04:28.460 --> 00:04:29.870
What's going on here?

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:33.250
Kunikida-san...

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:37.980
A lost cat, huh?

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.920
Did you really think things through
 before you brought it here?

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:46.720
Listen, it's a lot of responsibility
 to take care of a living thing.

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:50.170
You can't keep it on a whim.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:52.100
Kittens are especially delicate.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:55.960
You have to feed it special milk 
that's been warmed up.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:58.810
It can be neither too hot nor too cold.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:00.170
It must be about body temperature.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.940
It might have a weak stomach right now,
 so let's thin it down a little.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.000
Well?

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:06.960
A lot of work, isn't it?

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.120
Do you see what you're getting into?

00:05:08.120 --> 00:05:10.200
Kunikida-san's taking
 impeccable care of it!

00:05:10.510 --> 00:05:11.960
It's lapping...

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:12.700
You're right.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:16.780
Listen...

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.470
We can't keep it here forever.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:20.960
Is that not an option?

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.490
You know we can't
 guarantee its safety here.

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:26.590
There are times when no one is around, too.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.220
This isn't the place for a kitten.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:34.680
Boss.

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:37.850
<b>Mrowr</b>

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:39.750
Wh-Why...

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.500
<b>Cat Person</b>

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.460
Why is there a cat here?

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.230
<b>Cat Person</b>

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:45.060
How endearing...

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:45.640
No...

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:46.610
<b>Cat Person</b>

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.090
Let me redo my entry.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.710
I'll be right back.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.570
<b>Cat Person</b>

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:57.100
We might be able to keep it, 
but think about what's best for it.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:05:58.180
Okay...

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.320
<b>Found
Lost Cat</b>

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.320
<b>-Kitten
-Six whiskers
-Has a collar
-Likes people</b>

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.320
<b>Contact: ---</b>

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:24.320
<b>Armed
 Detective Agency</b>

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:27.930
I don't know how to thank you 
enough for taking care of her.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:28.740
Not at all.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.560
I missed you, Miiko!

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:35.150
I'm so sorry, Miiko.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:41.330
The kitten is well cared for.

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.250
I'm glad she has a place to call home.

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.120
Kyouka-chan...

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:49.680
We have a great cat, too.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.960
You should pet him 
whenever you're feeling down.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:55.010
I told you, I'm a <i>tiger!</i>

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:56.640
Meow!

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.610
<i>I never got a chance to pet it...</i>

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.650
<b>Cat Person</b>

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.650
<b>Episode 8</b>

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:07.650
<b>Rampo-san's Day 
Well Spent</b>

00:07:08.800 --> 00:07:09.900
Atsushi.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.390
Whatcha doing?

00:07:11.390 --> 00:07:13.410
I'm delivering this to the boss.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:15.930
You're taking him a rice cake?!

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.560
It's from a shop that's
 famous for being tasty.

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:20.330
I'll take it for you.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.290
But...

00:07:21.290 --> 00:07:23.380
Don't worry! I've got this!

00:07:25.100 --> 00:07:28.020
Snack time, boss.

00:07:29.230 --> 00:07:30.130
There you go.

00:07:30.460 --> 00:07:31.120
Thank you.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.010
<i>The rice cake has a bite taken out of it!</i>

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:38.200
Rampo.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:40.630
Did you take a bite?

00:07:42.970 --> 00:07:44.280
What are you talking about?

00:07:44.280 --> 00:07:45.000
Urp.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:50.780
I was looking forward to the rice cakes
 I heard we'd be getting today.

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:52.890
Alas, look at this!

00:07:52.890 --> 00:07:54.910
My precious first bite!

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:56.020
I see.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:57.980
This is rice cake assault.

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:02.000
What do you mean, assault?

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:03.600
It's deceased!

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.560
You'd best fess up now, Rampo.

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:21.520
<b>The plea bargain</b>

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:08.850
Why?! How?!

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:11.680
D-D-Do you have super deduction, too?

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:14.290
Compose yourself, great detective.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:16.600
Look at your own mouth.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:27.060
Don't you dare wipe it on my sleeve!

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:34.360
Boss, are you angry about the rice cake?

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:35.410
No.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.660
<i>I've been so busy, I forgot about it.</i>

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.480
I've kinda been reflecting on what I did.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:41.680
<i>"Kinda"?</i>

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.280
And I've been thinking,

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.850
since you're so busy, 
maybe I can do something for you.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:50.920
So, I asked Atsushi where he bought the rice cake, and I went there.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:52.290
Rampo!

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:53.690
I see.

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:56.760
You've bought me a new one.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.590
I told them our boss has been
 wanting to eat there.

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.450
This shop is my boss' favorite, y'know.

00:09:05.450 --> 00:09:07.440
My, my. Thank you, dear.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:09.490
You told her? That's it?

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:11.000
Yeah. And also...

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:12.350
There's more?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:15.820
I replied to all those letters
 you've been getting.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:20.080
<b>President 
Fukuzawa 
Yukichi</b>

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.660
These are important sealed documents

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.080
from government officials
 and important corporate figures!

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:22.680
<i>This incident could deal
 a serious blow to our company.</i>

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.830
<i>What would you advise, 
Fukuzawa-sensei?</i>

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:36.470
<b>Do whatever, I guess?</b>

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:25.940
Do whatever, I guess?

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.660
<i>We would like your input, sir.</i>

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:36.470
<b>I got nothing</b>

00:09:29.660 --> 00:09:30.560
I got nothing.

00:09:31.020 --> 00:09:33.090
<i>We implore you to attend our meeting.</i>

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:36.470
<b>I'll go if it 
seems fun</b>

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.990
I'll go if it seems fun.

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:41.760
<b>Whatever's 
easier</b>

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:44.520
<b>Sounds like
 a pain</b>

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:44.980
<b>Oh, really?</b>

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:46.980
<b>I guess?</b>

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:41.190
<i>I've been putting off replying to these 
letters because they're so difficult...</i>

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:46.980
<b>Meh</b>

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:44.790
<i>Rampo seems to have read
 my mind as always.</i>

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.980
<i>Should I just send these letters out?</i>

00:09:47.290 --> 00:09:49.780
I hope you haven't done anything else.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.680
Well, lastly, your phone...

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:53.480
My phone?!

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:56.510
<i>My phone has many important 
messages and contacts!</i>

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:57.790
<i>What have you done?!</i>

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.490
<b>XX 
Company</b>

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.600
I changed the ringtone to a cat mewing.

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:04.320
Ah.

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:05.230
Huh.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.600
<i>Fukuzawa Yukichi couldn't 
help but appreciate it.</i>

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.000
<b>Cat Person</b>

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:33.940
Dazai, quit playing around 
and get back to wrok.

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:36.430
A child's work is to play.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:38.650
You're a grown man! Now go!

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:43.990
Getting yelled at makes me sleepy.
Wake me up later, mom.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.450
I'm not your mother!
